        "model": "bai/qwen3.8-flash",
        "v": 5,
        "title": "Add referral system, bonus credits, and env var refactor",
        "summary": "Implemented a full referral system allowing users to generate unique links and earn 500 bonus credits per successful referral, capped at 5 referrals. This required new database tables for tracking referral status, API routes for code validation, and UI pages for user management. Environment variables were refactored from `APP_URL` to `NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL` across backend and web configs, and local development credit limits were significantly increased to bypass quota checks during testing.",
        "significance": "major",
        "at": "2026-09-15T18:43:18.852Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "You can now invite friends using a personal referral link and earn 500 bonus credits for each friend who signs up, up to a maximum of 5 successful referrals. A new section in the app shows your referral links and tracks how many bonuses you've earned. Behind the scenes, the team also switched how the app's web address is stored in configuration (renamed an internal setting) and raised the testing credit limits so developers can experiment without hitting usage caps, which only affects local development environments.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 4,
        "src": "a60b52e7d06c",
        "at": "2026-09-17T21:23:03.788Z"
      },
      "structured": {
