        "v": 5,
        "title": "Extract redeemReferralCode to helpers.ts and fix build errors",
        "summary": "Moved redeemReferralCode logic from web/src/app/api/referrals/route.ts to new file web/src/app/api/referrals/helpers.ts. Updated imports in route.ts and web/src/app/onboard/page.tsx to point to the new helper location. Fixed React build errors by escaping apostrophes in JSX text across web/src/app/referrals/page.tsx, web/src/app/referrals/[code]/page.tsx, and web/src/app/onboard/page.tsx. Replaced raw img tag with next/image component in web/src/components/navbar/sign-in-button.tsx.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "at": "2026-09-15T18:43:20.267Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "The referral program's credit-awarding logic was moved into its own file so it can be reused by both the sign-up page and the referral redemption endpoint, keeping the behavior consistent everywhere the feature appears. While doing that, several pages were fixed so that apostrophes in messages display correctly instead of breaking the site's build, a sign-in button now uses the site's standard image component for faster loading, and an error message about using your own referral code was cleaned up. These changes affect anyone signing up with a referral code and anyone visiting the referral pages, who will now see properly displayed text and consistent credit rewards.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
